trength while ignoring serious concerns. B's communication concerns are not evidenced, but still a risk. C's egocentric and unwillingness to develop are concerns. A's unorganized and poor criticism handling are concerns. D's arrogance and weak leadership are concerns.\n\nThus B still seems best overall. As Agent 1, we can support B, adding that B's technical competence (weather assessment, computer) is essential for long-distance flights, and his stress handling is proven. Also note that while we lack evidence of crew impact, the other candidates have more concrete concerns (A's unorganized, C's egocentric, D's arrogance). So we maintain recommendation B.\n\nWe need to reference discussion: agree with Agent 2 and 3, mention that we have no evidence of B's communication causing crew issues, and that other candidates have more serious concerns.\n\nThus public message: \"I agree with Agents 2 and 3, maintain recommendation for B, because...\"\n\nWe need to include explicit facts: B is very conscientious, handles stress well, good at assessing weather, excellent computer skills. Also note that B can be grumpy/uncooperative but no observed impact.\n\nThus vote B.\n\nNow produce output."}
